{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/106837-lucy-supergod-and-more-inspiration-for-aberrant","id":106837,"title":"Lucy, Supergod and more - Inspiration for Aberrant","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-04-06T05:04:03-07:00","id":106837,"title":"Lucy, Supergod and more - Inspiration for Aberrant","content":"So this trailer came out;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=2ICrNHF4o3Q\" data-code=\"2ICrNHF4o3Q\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/2ICrNHF4o3Q/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Now, obviously the 10% of the brain thing is silly and also the origin of Lucy's powers is not what we would see in a game of Aberrant.<br /> <br /> But in terms of the powers displayed (the bit where she just makes all those people go unconscious, or reads the worlds communications, and does telekinesis and so on), and also in terms of the disassociation the protagonist apparently seems to feel from humanity, this is Aberrant material right here. I mean, there's always been a strong transhumanist element to Aberrant and this movie seems like it might very much explore that. Reminds me of Akira in some ways.<br /> <br /> Thoughts? Is this the kind of thing people have in mind when they think of Aberrant? It is for me. This is kind of one end of the scale of what a Nova might be like, and then on the other end you have Warren Ellis' incomprehensible beings in Supergod. I think there is far more source material for the designers to work on than when the first edition of the game came out. So let's talk about what inspiration we will be drawing on when we make our campaigns and characters!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T06:18:12-07:00","id":106861,"title":"","content":"That's an excellent example of what a high-taint nova can be like WITHOUT having to resort to mercury tentacles. She herself even notes that she accumulating Taint so quickly, that she can notice her growing dissociation from humanity. Showed it to a friend of mine a few days ago; he's getting ready to run a Teragen game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T13:50:31-07:00","id":107063,"title":"","content":"I agree, and I hope that taint in terms of mental issues isn't just the typical RPG ones like paranoia and megalomania and so on. I'd like to see a whole bunch of mental aberrations related to actually being a Nova, which is better at making Novas <i>Inhuman</i> without making them insane. <br /> <br /> Also with regards to further inspiration, has anyone here heard of the comic book series <b>Uber</b>? It's an intelligent if horrific look at the closing days of WWII, where history suddenly shifts due to the development of human super-weapons. Not exploitative and very considered, it's worth reading just for Kieron Gillen's (the writer) insights into his writing and thought process on superhuman weapons and how their psyches might develop. I'd post a cover but you know I actually can't find one which is not so violent as to be potentially trigger-y.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T14:17:42-07:00","id":107075,"title":"","content":"With regards to Taint being dehumanizing instead of just plain crazy, I had a nova that erupted during a plane crash shortly after takeoff. He erupted with Mega Stamina 5, Armor (Impervious) 5, and a crapton of health levels and Taint. Wound up looking like a giant anthropomorphic alligator; his name is Sean. Sean's Taint revealed itself as being in a constant state of worry regarding everyone around him. After years of having Armor and Mega Stamina at his levels, he <i>forgot what it was like to feel pain or suffer illness</i>. If he ever had people over, he was <i>constantly</i> offering them food and beverages, because he couldn't remember how frequently normal people get hungry and thirsty. He carried around first aid kits everywhere, because <i>any </i>injury is bad, right? That needs to get checked out! Here, I've got some medicine for that! If anyone around him even had the sniffles, he'd offer to do everything for them while they stayed in bed. His Taint was that he couldn't <i>remember</i> what being human was like, and it was kind of obvious to the people around him. Hence, the social penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T14:36:12-07:00","id":107080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lustral_star</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/106837-lucy-supergod-and-more-inspiration-for-aberrant?p=107075#post107075\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With regards to Taint being dehumanizing instead of just plain crazy, I had a nova that erupted during a plane crash shortly after takeoff. He erupted with Mega Stamina 5, Armor (Impervious) 5, and a crapton of health levels and Taint. Wound up looking like a giant anthropomorphic alligator; his name is Sean. Sean's Taint revealed itself as being in a constant state of worry regarding everyone around him. After years of having Armor and Mega Stamina at his levels, he <i>forgot what it was like to feel pain or suffer illness</i>. If he ever had people over, he was <i>constantly</i> offering them food and beverages, because he couldn't remember how frequently normal people get hungry and thirsty. He carried around first aid kits everywhere, because <i>any </i>injury is bad, right? That needs to get checked out! Here, I've got some medicine for that! If anyone around him even had the sniffles, he'd offer to do everything for them while they stayed in bed. His Taint was that he couldn't <i>remember</i> what being human was like, and it was kind of obvious to the people around him. Hence, the social penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Awwwww man<br /> <br /> That just makes me want to give that alligator a hug.<br /> <br /> But yeah I think it's important to remember that, like Sean, Novas are often <i>aware</i> of how they have changed, and how they feel disassociated, and they think about how they want to deal with that. If you're a Nova that doesn't need to eat and drink but can, you may do so just because it makes you feel more human.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T14:40:33-07:00","id":107087,"title":"","content":"Hugs. So many hugs. EVERYONE wants to give Sean a hug in my group.<br /> <br /> But yes, he often forced himself to eat meals as a purely social thing -- he doesn't want to feel left out! And sleep was a difficult thing for him; many of his romantic pursuits didn't end well. The effects of Mega Stamina 5 (and above, in later games) on a romantic encounter are... well, obvious, if one thinks about it. But the fact that he often couldn't bring himself to just sit around and <i>wait</i> for 8 hours while his partner slept meant that they'd often wake up to an empty bed. Not very conducive to an emotional attachment.<br /> <br /> Many novas, especially ones with Mega attributes, wind up the same. The exact causes vary from one to the other, but the end result is similar.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T14:44:10-07:00","id":107090,"title":"","content":"Yeah and I like that. It's an inherently bit of pathos for any Nova; Nearly everyone that you meet is going to be a human being, but your Godlike powers could easily erect a big barrier between you and them. And the thing is that the barrier is not impassable, but it requires work. Aberrant works fantastically for personal sub-plots (like all superhero RPGs, actually), because there is a natural element of complexity added in by simply who you are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/117-solar","name":"Solar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar117_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1267"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-06T15:27:09-07:00","id":107113,"title":"","content":"Those are the stories that I like most about Aberrant -- the superpowers and everything are <i>great</i>, sure, don't get me wrong. Quite a bit of fun. But the human element -- or, sometimes, the <i>in</i>human element -- is what keeps me talking about my characters and game sessions years after the fact. Sean had Permanent Power and no dots in Dormancy, and I purposefully avoided purchasing dots in it for the story it provided -- he couldn't just &quot;turn off&quot; the barriers he had between himself and other people. To try dealing with everything, he sought out the Teragen for Chrysalis. He wound up completely ditching the idea and running in the opposite direction, though, when he realized exactly what Chrysalis was and would do for him. Great story time.<br /> <br /> Probably the best mental image I have was one suggested by some friends. Sean has the most middle-class, boring midwestern family ever. Mom, dad, and a sister majoring in Liberal Arts. Imagine Thanksgiving dinner with the three of them, and an eight foot tall alligator. No words exchanged. Just... uncomfortable silence and almost-spoken ice breakers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2464-lustral_star","name":"lustral_star","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2464_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"302"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-14T04:34:06-07:00","id":112539,"title":"","content":"i got a lot if ideas fro Heroes. I threw out a lot of the metaplot and made it more &quot;humans discover their powers&quot; and not I AM A SUPER GOD AND YOU CAN ALL KISS MY FEET! One character ended up in a mental ward because he couldn't control his telepathy in the beginning.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=485\" data-tempid=\"temp_485_1538393298974_786\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1277-karpomatic","name":"karpomatic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1277_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"143"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-04-26T21:19:27-07:00","id":120135,"title":"","content":"Though i like the setting, factions &amp; etc too, the &quot;human x transhuman&quot; inner conflict almost every Nova must fight daily is indeed one of the game most appealing aspects.<br /> <br /> My 1rst Aberrant character - well, he was so terribly messy that explaining it makes more time than i feel like spending on him. A poor fool so desperate to be human while unintentionally being the more alien than many of the beings he despised. His worse moment was when he came to learn of the concept of Chrysalis and realizing to his horror that he knew it already. His own inner turmoil, the paradox of desperately wanting normalcy while knowing oneself as inhuman, it had reshaped him, years ago. He fought the Terats while unknowingly being a 2nd stage himself all along...<br /> <br /> And here the trailer because the old video was taken.<br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"http://www.youtube.com/watch?v=1oJR6Di0Eck\" data-code=\"1oJR6Di0Eck\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/1oJR6Di0Eck/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}